  "releaseNotes": "Version 2.1.0\n\nAdded: Unified Service Result & Controller Extension System\n\nIntroduced a new ServiceResult<T> class and ResultStatus enum to standardize all service-layer responses.\n\nThis change replaces exception-driven flow in controllers with a consistent, type-safe response model.\n\nAdded a ControllerExtension helper that maps ServiceResult<T> outcomes to appropriate HTTP responses.\n\nImproved separation of concerns:\n\nThe Application layer now returns logical statuses (e.g., Success, Invalid, Unauthorized) instead of HTTP-specific codes.\n\nThe Web/API layer maps those statuses to correct HTTP results (e.g., 200 OK, 400 Bad Request, 401 Unauthorized, etc.).\n\nBenefits:\n\nCleaner, more predictable controller logic\n\nEasier testing and error handling\n\nReusable service responses across APIs, background jobs, and other integration points",
